    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b1ae1dd7_8a794344",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 90,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-23T17:19:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is the below check insufficient to keep DP entry from misbehaving? Or will we just enter mode and then exit on the power state change?\n\nIf this is a bug fix for the existing code, it should be its own CL.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 83,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 90,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "37bd178a2d4953258ecc573f40788501264c3dce",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4c02a4a6_fe2f42f8",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 90,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-24T02:32:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So perhaps it should be a separate fix, but it\u0027s really part of the fix for the same problem, which is that sometimes processes are started when the CPU is on, and then take some time (e.g discovery, DP alt mode negotiation), and by the time they complete, the CPU is off because the CPU had a power or state transition (either CPU on-\u003eoff or off-\u003eon)\nSome of this manifests in weird ways that I am not sure is deliberate or not.\nE.g in handle_new_power_state (common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c) it calls pe_exit_dp_mode, which calls pd_dfp_exit_mode, which exits the mode by clearing the opos in the mode data. This means discovery will have to run again in order for this mode to be reinitialised. So if this runs while dpm_attempt_mode_entry is also being run periodically, you can get a situation when it appears discovery has been run, but no DP mode exists (because the mode opos has been cleared), and mode_entry_done is set, and the mode is never entered.\n\nSo that is what I meant about state being out of sync, and most of it is caused by CPU power transitions forcing state changes during existing negoitations.\n\nA longer term fix is to really, really separate discovery from any kind of mode entry and exit, and have clear rules for how power transitions deal with the state data.\nI really didn\u0027t want to take on such a large refactor given the Puff schedule I\u0027m trying to meet, but I\u0027m happy to put some bandaids on until this can be done.",
      "parentUuid": "b1ae1dd7_8a794344",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 83,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 90,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "37bd178a2d4953258ecc573f40788501264c3dce",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b8d550f4_c6ad3fc6",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 90,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-24T16:00:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s definitely good to get something working consistently in for now.\n\nUltimately, the kernel handling our DP mode entry in the future should address a number of these issues.  Adding pd_partner_reset() should help as well to ensure we\u0027re starting with fresh connections on resets.",
      "parentUuid": "4c02a4a6_fe2f42f8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 83,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 90,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "37bd178a2d4953258ecc573f40788501264c3dce",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "014f34a1_222debb7",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 90,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-24T16:08:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e E.g in handle_new_power_state (common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c) it calls pe_exit_dp_mode, which calls pd_dfp_exit_mode, which exits the mode by clearing the opos in the mode data. This means discovery will have to run again in order for this mode to be reinitialised. So if this runs while dpm_attempt_mode_entry is also being run periodically, you can get a situation when it appears discovery has been run, but no DP mode exists (because the mode opos has been cleared), and mode_entry_done is set, and the mode is never entered.\n\nThis is a bug that should be fixed, although I think your bandaid takes the edge off for now. Because pe_exit_dp_mode is called from outside of the PE, and it doesn\u0027t care what state the PE is in or do any synchronization, it has the potential to corrupt the PE state, e.g. delete discovery data while we\u0027re trying to enter modes. Probably, pe_exit_dp_mode should set a flag that is then checked before doing a lot of stuff, especially discovery or mode entry. This has been the case for a long time, but I think recent changes have aggravated it. For one thing, we were never actually sending the Exit Mode until you fixed that bug. Also, as we have moved from a message-driven to a state-driven discovery/mode setup process, we have become more dependent on the consistency of our data structures.",
      "parentUuid": "4c02a4a6_fe2f42f8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 83,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 90,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "37bd178a2d4953258ecc573f40788501264c3dce",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
